+### User Story 2 - Server-Authoritative Auto Battles (Priority: P2)
+
+The system runs best-of-three auto battles using only saved attributes and a single RNG seed, streams each damage event to the UI, and shows inline round summaries so judges can verify outcomes without downloading replays.
+
+**Principles & Evidence**: Deterministic Auto-Battle Loop (server log mirrors UI timeline), Skill Evolution Guardrails (upgrade deltas recorded), Demo Readiness (spectator HUD referencing live events).  
+**Why this priority**: Judges must see fair, reproducible combat with clear on-screen evidence even in a lightweight demo.  
+**Independent Test**: Trigger an automated duel using stored monsters/skills, assert the battle log emitted by the API matches the UI summary timeline, and verify results remain deterministic when re-running with the same seed.
+
+**Acceptance Scenarios**:
+
+1. **Given** the system has saved monsters/skills for both players, **When** a round starts, **Then** the server simulates damage using the RNG seed, streams events to clients, and logs each hit/KO so the on-screen timeline reflects the authoritative source.
+2. **Given** a round finishes, **When** a judge expands the inline summary, **Then** the UI shows the same KO order, damage totals, and overtime flags recorded by the server log with no need to download a replay file.
*** End Patch
